        "code": {
          "text": "Reported left eye symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Five days after injury, symptoms are much improved, with mild intermittent scratchy sensation and awareness of the left eye, especially at the end of the work day. No significant pain, photophobia, or purulent discharge. Vision reported back to normal. No flashes, floaters, curtain, or significant blur. No fever or systemic symptoms."
      }
